44:     * 【35†Annual Reports】\nL45:   * 【6†Governance】\nL46:     * 【6†Governance Documents】\nL47:     * 【36†Committee Composition】\nL48:   * 【7†Investor Resources】\nL49:     * 【7†Investor FAQs】\nL50:     * 【37†Settlement Information】\nL51:     * 【14†Contact Us†www.ionis.com】\nL52:   * 【8†Scientific Publications & Presentations†ionis.com】\nL53:   * 【38†Investor Email Alerts】\nL54: Investor contact\nL55: \nL56: 760-603-2331\nL57: \nL58: Email (ir@ionis.com)\nL59: \nL60: Media contact\nL61: \nL62: 760-603-4679\nL63: \nL64: Email (media@ionis.com)\nL65: # Release Details\nL66: ##\nL67: \nL68: Ionis reports third quarter 2026 financial results and highlights progress on key programs\nL69: \nL70: November 9, 2026\nL71: \nL72: 【39†PDF Version】\nL73: \nL74: – ZANVASTRO^{™} (zilganersen) first approved medicine for Alexander disease; first independent launch underway from leading neurology pipeline –\nL75: \nL76: – TRYNGOLZA^{® }(olezarsen) 2026 product sales guidance lowered as sHTG launch ramps more gradually than expected reflecting early dynamics of establishing a new treatment paradigm –\nL77: – DAWNZERA^{® }(donidalorsen) launch momentum continues; reaffirming 2026 product revenue guidance –\nL78: \nL79: – Reaffirming 2026 total revenue, operating loss and cash guidance –\nL80: \nL81: CARLSBAD, Calif.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Nov. 9, 2026-- Ionis Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (Nasdaq: IONS) (the “Company”) today reported financial results and provided key updates for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026.\nL82: “In 2026, we continue to advance innovative medicines for people with serious diseases, underscored by three approvals for groundbreaking first-in-class medicines, two of which are Ionis-owned,” said Brett P. Monia, Ph.D., chief executive officer of Ionis. “TRYNGOLZA, our first launch in a large indication, represents a new treatment paradigm for the underserved sHTG population. While initial sales progress has been more gradual than anticipated, we are encouraged by the underlying launch fundamentals.\n"
